kadie@cs.uiuc.edu (Carl M Kadie) writes:


>>"8:00  Talking Point
>>       Host David Inge moderates a disucssion of censorship in
>>       society. Viewers are invited to call with their questions or
>>       comments."

By request. Here is a transcript of my 64.63 seconds:

["uhs" and "kind of"'s removed.]
=============================================

[... A few minutes of other folks, then Dean O'Shaughnessey telling
why some university speech restrictions are a pretty neat idea, then
...]

[Bit 1. Me sitting in front of my Sun workstation at work. It is
running the Life screen saver.]

"And the problem is that a university there is going to be lots of
offensive speech. In fact, at a university to do its mission, which
among other things is to find truth, some people are going to have to
say things that other people are going to find offensive."

[Cut away. Display of another computer (a color PC, I think) looking
at the subject lines of, I think, alt.sex. The most noticeable subject
line is "Are my cats gay lovers?". Voice of reporter:]

"Carl Kadie's concern go beyond the world of the classroom and into
the new world of Cyberspace. Each new technology forces us to face the
old question: what limits do we put on freedom of expression. In the
computer world that debate is on going."

[Bit 2. Me again.]

"The computer net because it is new and because it is based on
technology and new machines, it is often treated more like lab
equipment, like a PH meter in the chemistry room, than as a new forum
or medium, which it is. So, for example, a university that wouldn't
think about of censoring their library might, and have and fact,
censored their computer forums."

[End of my bits.]
